  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective systems for social dialogue and tripartism in place, institutionalised and operationalised</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Sri Lanka, weak tripartite dialogue and social partner engagement constrain consensus on labour reforms and crisis response. Outdated labour laws, weak enforcement of collective agreements, and fragmented labour governance undermine fair wage-setting and decent work, particularly for vulnerable and informal workers, including women and youth.

The ILO supports workers, employers, and government institutions by strengthening social dialogue and labour governance, and promoting evidence-based policies aligned with Convention No. 131 on minimum wage fixing to reduce gender pay gaps and improve dispute resolution. The intervention is led by the Ministry of Labour in partnership with social partners and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
